<FieldNotesLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <div class="legal-page">
    <p class="overline">Last updated: 26 Jan, 2024</p>
    <h1>BiomEdit Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p>This Privacy Policy reflects our policy when it comes to the purpose, use, and sharing of information collected via the Website in the course of conducting BiomEdit business, including your personal information. We strive to provide our users with a personalized and meaningful experience. However, we understand and appreciate that you want us to be considerate about what information we collect and about how that information may be used or shared. BiomEdit will, and will cause its affiliates to, establish and maintain business procedures that are consistent with this policy.</p>

      <h2>We respect the privacy rights of all individuals.</h2>
      <p>BiomEdit takes privacy seriously and is committed to complying with legal requirements regarding the privacy of personal information. BiomEdit will, from time to time, review its personal information collection, use, and disclosure practices to assure compliance with laws and regulations.</p>

      <h2>We do not collect your Personal Information.</h2>
      <p>BiomEdit does not collect your personal information when you visit our Website. BiomEdit will provide notice in the future, if personal information would be collected consistent with applicable law. In such a future situation, all notices provided will explain the need for the information and describe how the information will be used.</p>

      <h2>We may automatically collect and store certain technical information for Website management and security purposes.</h2>
      <p>Our Website does not collect any personal information from you. We may collect and store certain technical information for use in website management and security purposes. This type of information is limited and includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The Internet domain from which you access our Website.</li>
        <li>The IP address (a unique number for each computer connected to the Internet) from which you access our Website or services.</li>
        <li>The type of browser (e.g., Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Internet Explorer) used to access our Website.</li>
        <li>The operating system (Windows, Mac) used to access our Website or services.</li>
        <li>The date and time of visits.</li>
        <li>The URLs of the pages you visit, including advertisements or content we may suggest or direct you to.</li>
        <li>Your username, if it was used to log in.</li>
        <li>The URL of the forwarding site, if you visited our Website from another site.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>BiomEdit does not collect and will not sell your Personal Information to third parties for marketing purposes. Any other information gathered by BiomEdit (i.e., non-identifiable information such as IP addresses or other information gathered by our web logs or cookies) may be included in databases owned and maintained by BiomEdit or its agents. We retain all rights to these databases and the information contained in them.</p>

      <h2>We responsibly use Cookies to enhance the Website experience.</h2>
      <p>Our Website Uses Cookies. Cookies are text files containing small amounts of information which are downloaded to your device when you visit a website. Cookies provide a way for the website to recognize you, keep track of your preferences, and provide information to the website owners which may be used to improve your online experience. Your computer will only share the information in the cookie with the website that provided it, and no other website can request it. There are two types of cookies, session and persistent. Session cookies last only as long as your web browser is open. Once you close your browser, the cookie disappears. Persistent cookies store information on your computer for longer periods of time. Cookies are created not only by the BiomEdit website the user is browsing (namely &lsquo;first-party cookies&rsquo;) but also by other websites that run ads, widgets, or other elements on the page being loaded (namely &lsquo;third party cookies&rsquo;).</p>
      <p>Our Website may use session cookies for technical purposes such as to enable better and faster navigation through the site, or to allow you to customize your preferences for interacting with the site. Our Website may also use persistent cookies to remember you between visits so, for example, you can save your customized preference settings for future visits. We clearly identify where the Website uses persistent cookies and your ability to decline that use.</p>
      <p>Our cookies do not gather any confidential information from your hard drive. And at no time is your private information, whether stored in persistent cookies or elsewhere, shared with third parties who have no right to that information. If you do not wish to have session or persistent cookies stored on your machine, you can turn them off in your browser. However, this may affect the functioning of some of the Website features.</p>
      <p>To safeguard our websites and web applications, we may also use tools to prevent BOT attacks (i.e., cyber-attacks that use automated scripts to manipulate, disrupt or defraud websites and web applications) that may involve cookies or analytics associated with cookies.</p>
      <p>To help us analyze how users interact with our Website, we may use Google Analytics (and other tools), which is a service provided by Google, Inc. that uses cookies. Google Analytics collects information that helps us analyze how a user interacts with the Website, such as where they came from, how much time they spent on the site or a particular page, what links they clicked, duration of their visit, and their IP address. Google Analytics does not collect any personal information that could be used to identify an individual, such as their name, phone number, address, Social Security number, or credit card information. By using the Website, you consent to the processing of data about you by Google in the manner and for the purposes set out above.</p>
      <p>Google Analytics provides an opt-out option using the Google Analytics Opt-Out Browser Add-On for users who do not want this information to be collected on their behalf. For more information about Google Analytics Opt-Out Browser Add-On, please click on the following link: <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.</p>
      <p>You may elect to not allow cookies from our Website. Our Website operates most effectively when cookies are accepted by the user. Most of the Website will still be visible to you if you elect not to allow cookies to be placed on your computer; however, as mentioned previously, certain functions may not be available. For more information on how to control and delete your browser cookies, please refer to <a href="http://www.aboutcookies.org/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutcookies.org</a>.</p>

      <h2>We retain the flexibility to change this policy.</h2>
      <p>BiomEdit reserves the right to modify and update this policy or its related business practices at any time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</FieldNotesLayout>

